{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_slater_slater_occupation_identity", "label": "Slater occupation identity D = int_0^1 g_c(q) dq", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-SLATER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Along the stationary path in own-shell occupation q at fixed core and Z, with g_c(q) = eps_c(q) + (1/2) u_cc(q). If it holds, S and P are each a difference of integrals of ONE field eigen-quantity and the 0.88 is a ratio of such integrals."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_slater_half_u_term", "label": "The (1/2) u_cc term in dE/dq", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-SLATER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The functional carries (1/2) q(q-1) u_cc and eps_c already carries (q-1) u_cc, so dE/dq = eps_c + u_cc/2. J2 is filed as a LEVER that this term is real: |D - int eps_c dq| > 1e-3 Ha with a positive gap, and forcing u_cc to 0 must trip the identity check (rc=4)."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_slater_relaxation_as_curvature", "label": "Relaxation as q-curvature, not a separate object", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-SLATER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rel = (1/2) u_cc(1) - [g(1) - int g dq]: both terms are signed field outputs, so no responder decomposition is needed and the named residues of items 1-2 dissolve into the curvature of g in q. The no-adjustment rule is stated: if J1 fails, report which leg from the residual's q-dependence and do not adjust the integrand after the fact."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_slater_slater_occupation_identity", "target": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_janak_janak_slater_relation", "r